429685001-920bf163-22e1-4e2d-a665-470a77f58e1c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"31742bbec2390bed4b5e9db89cee3bceb5db03514300d1a9ddafcd41e7894c76","event_uuid":"f517b6f6-9874-45c9-a72b-78db6515107a","position":{"commit_sha":null,"position":"1786473482897120715-f517b6f6-9874-45c9-a72b-78db6515107a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1786471278890056001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f517b6f6-9874-45c9-a72b-78db6515107a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"671c-b741-664a-4b26"}],"description":"## Context\n\n`model_max_output_tokens` (`src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py`, `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`) knows only the three Claude ladder models and falls back to `DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS` (16,000) for an unmapped model. Amazon Nova models on Bedrock accept at most 10,000 output tokens, so every review call that rides the \"raise to model max\" seam with a Nova model is rejected by Bedrock with `ValidationException: The maximum tokens you requested exceeds the model limit of 10000` before it runs — measured live during the 2026-08-11 model-comparison experiments (rebar ticket b902-18af-14ed-4da1), where the whole plan-review LLM phase collapsed to INDETERMINATE until the table was patched in-process. Nova Pro subsequently completed 8/8 end-to-end plan-review replays, so the ceiling entry is the only blocker to running these models through rebar.\n\n## Plan\n\nAdd four entries to `MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS`: `(\"nova-pro\", 10_000)`, `(\"nova-2-lite\", 10_000)`, `(\"nova-lite\", 10_000)`, `(\"nova-micro\", 10_000)`. The lookup is a plain substring match, and `nova-lite` is NOT a substring of `nova-2-lite` (the `-2-` breaks it), so both forms are listed explicitly; the full Bedrock inference-profile ids (`us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0` etc.) are covered by the same substring semantics. Values per the AWS Bedrock model documentation: Nova family max output tokens = 10,000. No behavior change for any currently-configured model: the table is consulted only when the resolved model matches an entry, and the existing conservative fallback stays for everything else.\n\nExtend the existing unit coverage of `model_max_output_tokens` with the Nova ids (full Bedrock profile-id form and bare form).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `model_max_output_tokens(\"bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0\")` returns 10000. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -c \"import sys; sys.path.insert(0,'src'); from rebar.llm.review_kernel.verify import model_max_output_tokens as f; assert f('bedrock:us.amazon.nova-pro-v1:0')==10000 and f('us.amazon.nova-2-lite-v1:0')==10000 and f('claude-sonnet-4-6')==128000\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] A unit test pins the Nova entries alongside the existing Claude entries. Verify: `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" python -m pytest tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py -x` passes.\n- [ ] Unknown models still fall back to the configured default (existing behavior pinned by an assertion in the same test). Verify: same pytest run passes.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/review_kernel/verify.py","reason":"add Nova entries to MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_max_tokens_model_ceiling_1019.py","reason":"pin Nova + fallback behavior"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","671c-b741-664a-4b26"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"ef168cd3-fe5f-421d-ac7b-b8e69eac46ca","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"e800-c107-d4ac-463b","ticket_type":"task","title":"Teach MODEL_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS the Amazon Nova output ceilings (10k) so Bedrock Nova calls stop 400ing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["c4edd147-7649-405e-94c3-da2bcc94d940","d422b356-7d0c-4268-ba3c-286932a8ed48","8d434091-5465-40ab-b3b9-b6ceadd7f344","82145e3d-c686-462b-aab1-6af3f1217b3d","67225f0e-e532-4b3e-a417-e2e939040aa0","5f5f2979-a26f-4f90-97f1-290fd73bdc7a","ef168cd3-fe5f-421d-ac7b-b8e69eac46ca","920bf163-22e1-4e2d-a665-470a77f58e1c","f517b6f6-9874-45c9-a72b-78db6515107a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786473482897120716,"uuid":"dc4e341c-8dac-4849-96c0-56ea02d7b71d"}